# Template for the private site file that install.sh reads.
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/certus
#   cp deploy/llm-d/site.env.example ~/.config/certus/llm-d-site.env
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/certus/llm-d-site.env
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/certus/llm-d-site.env      # fill in the REQUIRED values
#   DRY_RUN=1 deploy/llm-d/install.sh            # check it; changes nothing
#
# Or keep it anywhere else and point SITE_ENV at it. Several llm-d instances can
# share one cluster on disjoint nodes: give each its own site file with its own
# NAMESPACE and node lists, and pick it with SITE_ENV=<file>.
#
# Never commit a filled-in copy: it names real infrastructure (nodes, registry,
# how many GPUs sit where), and the committed profiles/ are kept free of that on
# purpose.
#
# Shell syntax, sourced by bash. Each line is `: "${VAR:=value}"`, which sets a
# default only, so `AGG_REPLICAS=2 deploy/llm-d/install.sh` still overrides it.
#
# The required values are deliberately left EMPTY. install.sh refuses to run
# until they are filled in, so a copied template cannot quietly deploy one
# replica and leave GPUs idle. Worked examples are in the "Setting up a new
# cluster" section of deploy/llm-d/README.md.
#
# To find the values, list the GPU nodes and their GPU counts:
#   kubectl get nodes -o custom-columns='NAME:.metadata.name,GPUS:.status.allocatable.nvidia\.com/gpu'

# --- Profile --------------------------------------------------------------
# Which committed profile matches this cluster's GPUs: a directory under
# deploy/llm-d/profiles/ (`ls deploy/llm-d/profiles`). Every engine in a profile
# uses one GPU of that type.
: "${PROFILE:=a30}"

# --- Instance ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The namespace is the instance's identity. install.sh labels the instance's
# nodes llm-d.ai/instance=<NAMESPACE>, confines its pods to them, and refuses a
# node another instance already holds. Change it for a second instance.
: "${NAMESPACE:=llm-d-quickstart}"

# --- Aggregated serving (the default; also WITH_CERTUS=1) -------------------
# REQUIRED. Space-separated nodes this instance serves on, from the NAME column.
: "${AGG_NODES:=}"
# REQUIRED. One replica per GPU: the sum of the GPUS of AGG_NODES.
: "${AGG_REPLICAS:=}"

# --- Prefill/decode disaggregation (PD=1) -----------------------------------
# REQUIRED for PD=1. Each replica takes one GPU, so prefill + decode should
# equal the GPU count. For long multi-turn chat give decode the larger share:
# decode GPUs hold every in-flight conversation's KV cache.
: "${PD_PREFILL_REPLICAS:=}"
: "${PD_DECODE_REPLICAS:=}"
# REQUIRED for PD=1. Space-separated node names from the NAME column.
# install.sh labels them llm-d.ai/pd-prefill=true / llm-d.ai/pd-decode=true,
# which is what the pd overlay selects on. The GPUs on each role's nodes must
# cover that role's replicas. A node may appear in both lists if it has GPUs for
# both. AGG_NODES and the PD lists may name different nodes. The instance holds
# whichever set the current layout uses, so switching between layouts with
# different sets needs RELEASE_NODES=1 to give up the nodes left behind.
: "${PD_PREFILL_NODES:=}"
: "${PD_DECODE_NODES:=}"

# --- certus offload image (WITH_CERTUS=1 only) ------------------------------
# Where publish-image.sh pushed the connector image: the same two values you
# ran it with. Leave commented out if you do not use WITH_CERTUS.
# : "${CERTUS_REGISTRY:=registry.example.com}"
# : "${CERTUS_REPO:=my-team-docker-local}"
